rust-vmm/vhost-device c0bfee92: the reader-thread change of upstream PR
rust-vmm/vhost-device#1020 (https://github.com/rust-vmm/vhost-device/pull/1020, open,
fixes #1009), backported onto this pin. Backport, drop on pin bump: apply it after
vhost-device-c0bfee92.patch (#924); once #1020 has merged and the pin contains it, delete
this file.

vhost-device-can's reader thread loops on a non-blocking CAN socket with nothing to wait
on, so one DomD vCPU runs at 100% even when the bus is idle (79 s of CPU in 80 s
wall, #1009). This waits for the socket with poll(2), for at most 100 ms, before every
read; on timeout the loop checks the exit status again, so the thread still stops within
100 ms. The wait does not hold the controller lock.

Why a backport and not #1020 as it is: #1020 is stacked on #937 ("use the same socket for
send/recv", open), which this pin does not have. At this pin the reader owns its own
socket (read_can_socket opens one), so the poll is on that socket's fd. Also adds libc to
vhost-device-can's dependencies (Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock; libc 0.2.189 is already in the
lock).

